[4.4277, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2KHere are six short points on how to test the Python cart function:                                  \r\n\r\n 1 Test normal prices by adding valid products to the cart with expected prices.                    \r\n 2 Verify that an empty cart is properly initialized with no items.                                 \r\n 3 Test decimal prices by adding products with valid decimal values to the cart.                    \r\n 4 Check that negative prices are handled correctly by adding products with negative values to the  \r\n   cart.                                                                                            \r\n 5 Test invalid input by attempting to add products to the cart with invalid data                   "]
[4.5126, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2KHere are six short points on how to test the Python cart function:                                  \r\n\r\n 1 Test normal prices by adding valid products to the cart with expected prices.                    \r\n 2 Verify that an empty cart is properly initialized with no items.                                 \r\n 3 Test decimal prices by adding products with valid decimal values to the cart.                    \r\n 4 Check that negative prices are handled correctly by adding products with negative values to the  \r\n   cart.                                                                                            \r\n 5 Test invalid input by attempting to add products to the cart with invalid data (e.g. negative    \r\n   quantity). 6                                                                                     "]
[4.5977, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2KHere are six short points on how to test the Python cart function:                                  \r\n\r\n 1 Test normal prices by adding valid products to the cart with expected prices.                    \r\n 2 Verify that an empty cart is properly initialized with no items.                                 \r\n 3 Test decimal prices by adding products with valid decimal values to the cart.                    \r\n 4 Check that negative prices are handled correctly by adding products with negative values to the  \r\n   cart.                                                                                            \r\n 5 Test invalid input by attempting to add products to the cart with invalid data (e.g. negative    \r\n   quantity).                                                                                       \r\n 6 Identify and test for regressions by re                                                          "]
[4.6825, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2KHere are six short points on how to test the Python cart function:                                  \r\n\r\n 1 Test normal prices by adding valid products to the cart with expected prices.                    \r\n 2 Verify that an empty cart is properly initialized with no items.                                 \r\n 3 Test decimal prices by adding products with valid decimal values to the cart.                    \r\n 4 Check that negative prices are handled correctly by adding products with negative values to the  \r\n   cart.                                                                                            \r\n 5 Test invalid input by attempting to add products to the cart with invalid data (e.g. negative    \r\n   quantity).                                                                                       \r\n 6 Identify and test for regressions by re-testing previously passed tests to ensure no changes     "]
[4.7246, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2KHere are six short points on how to test the Python cart function:                                  \r\n\r\n 1 Test normal prices by adding valid products to the cart with expected prices.                    \r\n 2 Verify that an empty cart is properly initialized with no items.                                 \r\n 3 Test decimal prices by adding products with valid decimal values to the cart.                    \r\n 4 Check that negative prices are handled correctly by adding products with negative values to the  \r\n   cart.                                                                                            \r\n 5 Test invalid input by attempting to add products to the cart with invalid data (e.g. negative    \r\n   quantity).                                                                                       \r\n 6 Identify and test for regressions by re-testing previously passed tests to ensure no changes     \r\n   broke existing functionality.                                                                    \r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
[4.7256, "o", "Here are six short points on how to test the Python cart function:                                  \r\n\r\n 1 Test normal prices by adding valid products to the cart with expected prices.                    \r\n 2 Verify that an empty cart is properly initialized with no items.                                 \r\n 3 Test decimal prices by adding products with valid decimal values to the cart.                    \r\n 4 Check that negative prices are handled correctly by adding products with negative values to the  \r\n   cart.                                                                                            \r\n 5 Test invalid input by attempting to add products to the cart with invalid data (e.g. negative    \r\n   quantity).                                                                                       \r\n 6 Identify and test for regressions by re-testing previously passed tests to ensure no changes     \r\n   broke existing functionality.                                                                    \r\n"]
